      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "First, we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 18 and 42.\n\nThe prime factorization of 18 is:\n\\[ 18 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\]\n\nThe prime factorization of 42 is:\n\\[ 42 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 7 \\]\n\nThe common factors are 2 and 3. Therefore, the GCD of 18 and 42 is:\n\\[ \\text{GCD} = 2 \\times 3 = 6 \\]\n\nNext, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of 18 and 42. The LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime that appears in the factorizations of the two numbers.\n\nThe prime factorizations are:\n\\[ 18 = 2^1 \\times 3^2 \\]\n\\[ 42 = 2^1 \\times 3^1 \\times 7^1 \\]\n\nThe LCM is:\n\\[ \\text{LCM} = 2^1 \\times 3^2 \\times 7^1 = 2 \\times 9 \\times 7 = 126 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the product of the GCD and the LCM:\n\\[ \\text{GCD} \\times \\text{LCM} = 6 \\times 126 = 756 \\]\n\nThus, the product of the greatest common divisor and the least common multiple of 18 and 42 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{756} \\]",
